# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Nexus QA — Multi-Tier LLM Provider Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Each engine supports 3 tiers of LLM providers with automatic failover:
#   Tier 1 (PRIMARY)  — Best cloud provider (highest quality)
#   Tier 2 (SECONDARY)— Cloud fallback (still good, different vendor)
#   Tier 3 (LOCAL)    — On-prem / local model (Ollama, vLLM, etc.)
#
# The system automatically falls back: Tier1 → Tier2 → Tier3
#
# USAGE:
#   1. Copy the variables you need into your .env or docker-compose
#   2. Set only the tiers you have access to (unused tiers are skipped)
#   3. On-prem deployments: just set _TIER3_ variables
#   4. Cloud deployments: set _TIER1_ and _TIER2_
#   5. Hybrid: set all three tiers for maximum resilience
#
# DEPLOYMENT MODES:
#   on-prem  = Only Tier 3 configured (local models, no internet)
#   cloud    = Only Tier 1/2 (API-based, no local infrastructure)
#   hybrid   = All tiers (best resilience, highest cost)
#
# The Brain Engine's /api/v1/brain/tiers endpoint shows active
# deployment mode and tier status across all engines.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Global Fallback (used when per-engine tiers not set) ──────
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Brain Engine (port 8011) — Intelligent Coordinator
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BRAIN_TIER1_PROVIDER=anthropic
# BRAIN_TIER1_MODEL=claude-opus-4-5-20250514
# BRAIN_TIER1_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# BRAIN_TIER2_PROVIDER=openai
# BRAIN_TIER2_MODEL=gpt-5
# BRAIN_TIER2_API_KEY=sk-...

# BRAIN_TIER3_PROVIDER=ollama
# BRAIN_TIER3_MODEL=llama3.1:70b

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
